# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Claude
.claude/

# Research & design documents live in the private Nimit-docs repo.
#
# Written `docs/*` and not `docs/`, deliberately: git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a later `!docs/store/` under a `docs/` rule re-includes
# nothing and fails silently. Excluding the contents instead leaves the door open
# for the one exception below.
docs/*

# ...which is docs/store/. That is not research — it is the text of pages that get
# PUBLISHED: the privacy policy, the support page, and the answers typed into App
# Store Connect. privacy.md's own rule is "if the app changes, this page changes in
# the same commit", and a page whose words live on one laptop cannot obey it.
# Nothing in it is secret; all of it is written to be read by strangers. The scans,
# the market research and the Nimit-docs drafts stay excluded.
!docs/store/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Git history is effectively permanent — a secret or
# a copyrighted corpus committed here cannot be un-published by a later commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets. The Supabase anon key is public by design and lives in Actions
# variables; the service_role key bypasses RLS entirely and must never land here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
supabase/.env

# Supabase CLI local state
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/

# Database dumps may contain the editorial schema and user personal data
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bak

# Source corpus: copyrighted scans, transcriptions and import payloads.
# The import *scripts* belong in this repo; the content does not.
corpus/
content-payloads/

# Book-entry payloads: facts line by line, but a whole book systematically
# extracted is close to copying the publisher's table. Script public, corpus not.
supabase/seeds/incoming/*.tsv
!supabase/seeds/incoming/TEMPLATE.tsv

# Generated number SQL from owned books: same reasoning as the .tsv payloads.
supabase/seeds/incoming/*.sql
